## Why This Is Asked

To assess practical control-plane hardening choices under real-world friction, focusing on mobile app token misuse and multi-tenant isolation.

## Key Concepts

- OAuth2/OIDC security best practices (PKCE, short TTLs)
- Token binding and device fingerprinting
- Token rotation and per-tenant scopes
- Token introspection and revocation
- Observability and IR readiness

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: rotate refresh token on use and bind to device and tenant
function onRefresh(token, deviceId, tenant) {
  if (!isValidDevice(token.bindInfo, deviceId, tenant)) throw new Error('invalid');
  const newToken = issueAccessToken(tenant, token.tenant);
  rotateRefreshToken(token.id);
  return { accessToken: newToken, refreshToken: getRotatedRefresh(token.id) };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the token binding mechanism in CI/CD?
- What metrics indicate token abuse and how would you respond?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to apply practical logging security to prevent token leakage in fintech contexts, a common attack surface.

## Key Concepts
- Log data leakage risks
- Redaction and sanitization
- Middleware for request/response logs
- CI gates for secrets in code
- Incident response and key rotation

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactLog(obj){
  const redacted = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(obj), (k,v)=>{
    if (/token|secret|api_key|Authorization/i.test(k)) return "[REDACTED]";
    return v;
  });
  return JSON.stringify(redacted);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the redaction effectively?
- How would you handle binary payloads or proprietary log formats?
- What logging libraries and CI tools would you choose and why?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to apply multi-tenant isolation, data governance, and IR planning in a Databricks context beyond generic concepts.

## Key Concepts

- Unity Catalog RBAC and object-level permissions
- Tenant-scoped secret scopes and secret management
- Dynamic data masking and access controls for notebooks
- Audit logs and SIEM integration for detection
- Incident response playbooks and metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo policy enforcement in app layer
function authorize(user, dataset) {
  if (!user.tenants.includes(dataset.tenant)) throw new Error("Access denied");
  // additional masking rules could apply here
  return dataset;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test isolation guarantees across tenants? 
- What metrics and alerts would you instrument to detect leakage or misuse?
